An SDET implements this globally to log all network traffic for debugging. Suddenly, execution time inflates by 400%, and tests start timing out. What is the architectural bottleneck?

```typescript
await page.route('**/*', route => {
  console.log(route.request().url());
  route.continue();
});
```

**Options:**
- Using `**/*` intercepts absolutely every asset (images, fonts, CSS, JS). Routing every single sub-resource from the Chromium engine through the Node.js event loop and back creates a massive IPC (Inter-Process Communication) bottleneck.
- Playwright disables caching when `page.route` is active.
- The `console.log` method is asynchronous and slow.
- `route.continue()` modifies the headers automatically.
